Each single change is safe: every majority of the old list meets every majority of the new one, so the two can't decide different things. Two changes that both start from C are not. The last line of the first run is exactly the 2015 bug: S1 elected by {S1, S4, S5} under D, while E's entry was committed on {S2, S3}. The rule that a new leader commits its no-op first stops the second change from starting until the first one is settled, so the lists always differ by one server. The second run is the paper's jump from three to five: two old servers and three new ones can each form a majority.

